Sources
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Press is an independent implementation written against the IETF
specifications: RFC 3550 (RTP), RFC 3551 (RTP/AVP), RFC 2250 (MPEG-TS payload)
and RFC 2733 (generic FEC). The algorithms in RFC 3550's appendices (sequence
number validation, loss and jitter computation) are ported from the RFC's own
example code.

SMPTE 2022-1 is not freely available. Its FEC packet layout was confirmed
against the behaviour of two open implementations, used as references for the
wire format only. No code from either is included:

FFmpeg — libavformat/prompeg.c (Pro-MPEG CoP #3 FEC sender)
    https://ffmpeg.org, LGPL-2.1-or-later

GStreamer — rtpst2022-1-fecenc / rtpst2022-1-fecdec
    https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org, LGPL-2.1-or-later
